"""Original NumPy and pandas contracts, numerical examples and debugging cases."""
from python_guide_core import t

t(11,'array-shape','Read array shapes','shape describes the length of each axis; size counts all elements. Record both before choosing a reshape or reduction so axis semantics stay explicit.','Counting only rows is not the total element count.','a = np.asarray(data)\nresult = [list(a.shape),int(a.size)]',[([[1,2],[3,4]],[[2,2],4]),([[1,2,3]],[[1,3],3])],'int(a.size)','len(a)')
t(11,'array-dtype','Choose numeric dtypes','An explicit floating dtype preserves fractional values during array construction. Integer conversion truncates fractional parts and can change a model input contract.','An integer dtype silently discards these fractions.','result = np.asarray(data,dtype=np.float64).tolist()',[([1.5,2.5],[1.5,2.5]),([0.0],[0.0])],'dtype=np.float64','dtype=np.int64')
t(11,'array-broadcast','Broadcast along compatible trailing axes','Broadcasting compares dimensions from the right; each paired size must match or be one. A row vector can be applied to each matrix row without explicitly copying it.','Using only the first offset applies a scalar instead of the row offsets.','matrix,row = data\nresult = (np.asarray(matrix)+np.asarray(row)).tolist()',[([[[1,2],[3,4]],[10,20]],[[11,22],[13,24]]),([[[0,0]],[1,2]],[[1,2]])],'np.asarray(row)','np.asarray(row)[0]')
t(11,'array-basic-view','Basic slicing usually shares storage','A basic NumPy slice is normally a view. Mutating it can update the parent array; use copy when independent storage is the required contract.','An independent copy does not propagate writes back to its parent.','a = np.asarray(data)\nview = a[1:]\nview[:] = 0\nresult = a.tolist()',[([1,2,3],[1,0,0]),([4],[4])],'view = a[1:]','view = a[1:].copy()')
t(11,'advanced-index-copy','Advanced indexing creates a copy','Integer-array indexing selects values into a new array. Mutating that result does not update the original array; indexed assignment is a separate operation.','Replacing advanced indexing with a slice changes ownership.','a = np.asarray(data)\nb = a[[0,1]]\nb[:] = 0\nresult = a.tolist()',[([1,2,3],[1,2,3]),([4,5],[4,5])],'a[[0,1]]','a[:2]')
t(11,'array-mask','Boolean masks select records','A Boolean mask selects positions where the predicate is true. Parenthesize elementwise comparisons when combining them, and avoid Python scalar and/or on arrays.','Including zero changes a strictly-positive filter.','a = np.asarray(data)\nresult = a[a>0].tolist()',[([-1,0,2],[2]),([0],[])],'a>0','a>=0')
t(11,'reduction-axis','Reduction axes describe what disappears','Summing along axis zero collapses rows and retains one value per column. Summing along axis one instead produces one value per row.','Changing the reduction axis changes the meaning and often the output shape.','result = np.asarray(data).sum(axis=0).tolist()',[([[1,2],[3,4]],[4,6]),([[1,2,3]],[1,2,3])],'axis=0','axis=1')
t(11,'keepdims-contract','Keep dimensions for later broadcasting','keepdims retains reduced axes with length one. This makes the result broadcast back against the original array without accidentally aligning with another axis.','Dropping the axis changes a two-dimensional shape contract.','a = np.asarray(data)\nresult = a.sum(axis=1,keepdims=True).tolist()',[([[1,2],[3,4]],[[3],[7]]),([[0,1,2]],[[3]])],'keepdims=True','keepdims=False')
t(11,'ufunc-out','Write ufunc results into explicit output','A ufunc out parameter writes into supplied compatible storage. Choose a dtype that can represent the result and reason about aliasing before reusing buffers.','Multiplying instead of adding changes the transformation.','a = np.asarray(data,dtype=float)\nout = np.empty_like(a)\nnp.add(a,2,out=out)\nresult = out.tolist()',[([1,3],[3,5]),([],[])],'np.add(a,2,out=out)','np.multiply(a,2,out=out)')
t(11,'random-generator','Own a random generator','default_rng constructs an independent random generator. A fixed seed reproduces this generator sequence in the pinned environment, without establishing cross-version or GPU reproducibility.','Advancing only one generator breaks sequence agreement.','a = np.random.default_rng(data)\nb = np.random.default_rng(data)\nresult = bool(np.array_equal(a.integers(0,100000,size=8),b.integers(0,100000,size=8)))',[(7,True),(42,True)],'b = np.random.default_rng(data)','b = np.random.default_rng(data+1)')
t(11,'finite-values','Check nonfinite numeric values','isfinite rejects both infinities and NaNs. A missingness check alone does not reject every nonfinite value, so choose a predicate that matches the data contract.','Checking only for NaN admits infinite values.','a = np.asarray(data,dtype=float)\na = np.append(a,np.inf)\nresult = np.isfinite(a).tolist()',[([1,2],[True,True,False]),([],[False])],'np.isfinite(a)','~np.isnan(a)')

t(12,'reshape-size','Reshaping preserves element count','reshape changes dimensions while preserving the number of elements. A -1 dimension can be inferred when the remaining sizes divide the element count.','Changing the column count changes the resulting shape.','result = np.asarray(data).reshape(-1,2).tolist()',[([1,2,3,4],[[1,2],[3,4]]),([0,1],[[0,1]])],'reshape(-1,2)','reshape(-1,1)')
t(12,'array-strides','Strides describe memory steps','Array strides give byte increments along axes. A reversed view has a negative stride and can share storage without being C-contiguous.','Taking an unreversed copy changes the stride direction.','a = np.asarray(data,dtype=np.int64)\nb = a[::-1]\nresult = [int(b.strides[0]),bool(np.shares_memory(a,b))]',[([1,2,3],[-8,True]),([4,5],[-8,True])],'a[::-1]','a.copy()')
t(12,'matrix-product','Matrix multiplication differs from elementwise multiplication','The @ operator contracts the inner matrix dimension. Elementwise multiplication pairs corresponding entries and follows broadcasting rules rather than matrix-product rules.','Using * instead of @ computes a different operation.','a,b = map(np.asarray,data)\nresult = (a@b).tolist()',[([[[1,2],[3,4]],[[1,0],[0,1]]],[[1,2],[3,4]]),([[[1,1]],[[2],[3]]],[[5]])],'a@b','a*b')
t(12,'einsum-contract','Name contractions with einsum','einsum can express index contractions explicitly. Repeated labels identify a contracted axis; output labels identify axes preserved in the result.','Keeping the contracted label requests a different shape.','a,b = map(np.asarray,data)\nresult = np.einsum("ij,j->i",a,b).tolist()',[([[[1,2],[3,4]],[10,20]],[50,110]),([[[1,1]],[2,3]],[5])],'ij,j->i','ij,j->ij')
t(12,'linear-solve','Solve systems without explicitly inverting','linalg.solve computes a solution for a square nonsingular system. Check residuals and conditioning; a successful solve alone does not establish numerical reliability.','Multiplying the coefficient matrix by the target does not solve the system.','a,b = data\nresult = np.linalg.solve(np.asarray(a,dtype=float),np.asarray(b,dtype=float)).tolist()',[([[[2,0],[0,4]],[4,8]],[2,2]),([[[1]],[3]],[3])],'np.linalg.solve(np.asarray(a,dtype=float),np.asarray(b,dtype=float))','np.asarray(a)@np.asarray(b)')
t(12,'least-squares','Least squares handles overdetermined systems','lstsq minimizes squared residuals rather than requiring an exact square system. The returned coefficient vector must be interpreted alongside rank and singular values.','Replacing the fit with a zero coefficient vector ignores the data.','a,b = data\nresult = np.linalg.lstsq(np.asarray(a),np.asarray(b),rcond=None)[0].tolist()',[([[[1],[2],[3]],[2,4,6]],[2.0]),([[[1],[2]],[0,0]],[0.0])],'np.linalg.lstsq(np.asarray(a),np.asarray(b),rcond=None)[0]','np.zeros(len(a[0]))')
t(12,'svd-rank','Singular values reveal numerical rank','SVD factors a matrix into orthogonal directions and nonnegative singular values. Numerical rank uses a tolerance; exact symbolic rank and floating rank are different claims.','Counting every dimension as independent ignores rank deficiency.','result = int(np.linalg.matrix_rank(np.asarray(data)))',[([[1,2],[2,4]],1),([[1,0],[0,1]],2)],'int(np.linalg.matrix_rank(np.asarray(data)))','len(data)')
t(12,'fft-spectrum','FFT coefficients have a frequency interpretation','The FFT transforms a sequence into complex frequency coefficients. A constant signal has only a DC component under this unnormalized forward convention.','Returning input magnitudes instead of spectral magnitudes changes domains.','result = np.abs(np.fft.fft(np.asarray(data))).round(8).tolist()',[([1,1,1,1],[4,0,0,0]),([0,0],[0,0])],'np.fft.fft(np.asarray(data))','np.asarray(data)')
t(12,'integer-overflow','Integer dtypes have finite ranges','A fixed-width NumPy integer wraps according to its dtype arithmetic. Promote before an operation if the mathematical result must fit; promotion afterward cannot recover overflowed bits.','Casting only after multiplication preserves an already-overflowed value.','a = np.asarray(data,dtype=np.int8)\nresult = (a.astype(np.int64)*2).tolist()',[([100,-100],[200,-200]),([1],[2])],'a.astype(np.int64)*2','(a*2).astype(np.int64)')
t(12,'masked-array','Keep missingness separate from values','A masked array excludes masked positions from reductions. Filling a masked value with zero before taking a mean changes the effective denominator.','Including masked zeros biases the mean.','values,mask = data\na = np.ma.array(values,mask=mask)\nresult = float(a.mean())',[([[2,100,4],[False,True,False]],3.0),([[1,3],[False,False]],2.0)],'float(a.mean())','float(a.filled(0).mean())')
t(12,'memmap-scope','Memory maps still own resources','memmap exposes file-backed array storage. Flush changes, release mappings before scope cleanup, and avoid assuming that memory mapping bounds every downstream allocation.','Writing a different value is still a successful file operation.','with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as directory:\n    path = Path(directory)/"values.bin"\n    mapped = np.memmap(path,dtype="float64",mode="w+",shape=(len(data),))\n    mapped[:] = data\n    mapped.flush()\n    result = mapped.tolist()\n    del mapped',[([1,2],[1.0,2.0]),([3],[3.0])],'mapped[:] = data','mapped[:] = 0','import tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path')

t(13,'series-labels','Series indexing has labels','loc selects labels while iloc selects integer positions. Integer-looking labels do not make these two interfaces interchangeable.','Position zero is not necessarily the requested label.','s = pd.Series(data,index=[10,20])\nresult = int(s.loc[20])',[([3,4],4),([0,9],9)],'s.loc[20]','s.iloc[0]')
t(13,'frame-columns','Select DataFrame columns by name','A DataFrame stores named columns with potentially different dtypes. A list of column names preserves two-dimensional structure even when selecting one column.','Selecting a scalar column name returns a Series with different shape.','frame = pd.DataFrame(data)\nresult = list(frame[["x"]].shape)',[({'x':[1,2],'y':[3,4]},[2,1]),({'x':[],'y':[]},[0,1])],'frame[["x"]]','frame["x"]')
t(13,'label-alignment','Arithmetic aligns labels','pandas arithmetic aligns by index labels rather than row position. Specify a fill policy deliberately when one side lacks a label.','Combining values positionally pairs different records.','a,b = data\nleft = pd.Series(a,index=["a","b"])\nright = pd.Series(b,index=["b","a"])\nresult = (left+right).tolist()',[([[1,2],[10,20]],[21,12]),([[0,0],[3,4]],[4,3])],'left+right','left+right.to_numpy()')
t(13,'missing-data','Missingness needs an explicit policy','fillna replaces missing entries using a chosen value. Filling with zero is a domain decision and must not silently substitute for a training-only imputation strategy.','Dropping missing rows changes row count and alignment.','result = pd.Series(data,dtype=float).fillna(0).tolist()',[([1,None,3],[1,0,3]),([None],[0])],'fillna(0)','dropna()')
t(13,'nullable-integers','Nullable integers preserve absent values','The Int64 extension dtype supports integer values with a missing sentinel. Fill or explicitly serialize missing entries before converting them into ordinary Python integers.','Using zero as the missing count understates absent records.','s = pd.Series(data,dtype="Int64")\nresult = [str(s.dtype),int(s.isna().sum())]',[([1,None],['Int64',1]),([2,3],['Int64',0])],'s.isna().sum()','0')
t(13,'string-operations','Vectorized strings need missing policies','The str accessor performs string operations elementwise. Set na explicitly when a Boolean predicate must have a definite result for missing text.','Treating missing text as a match changes filter membership.','result = pd.Series(data,dtype="string").str.contains("cat",regex=False,na=False).tolist()', [(['cat',None,'dog'],[True,False,False]),(['bobcat'],[True])],'na=False','na=True')
t(13,'categorical-codes','Categories define a finite vocabulary','Categorical codes refer to a declared category order and use -1 for missing or unknown values. The codes are not ordinal measurements unless the domain says so.','Reordering the vocabulary changes the numeric codes.','result = pd.Categorical(data,categories=["low","high"]).codes.tolist()',[(['high','low','other'],[1,0,-1]),(['low'],[0])],'["low","high"]','["high","low"]')
t(13,'join-cardinality','Validate join cardinality','A many-to-one merge requires unique keys on the right. Validate that assumption so duplicate lookup rows do not silently multiply training examples.','A many-to-many allowance accepts unintended row expansion.','left = pd.DataFrame({"id":data})\nright = pd.DataFrame({"id":[1,1],"value":[2,3]})\ntry:\n    left.merge(right,on="id",validate="many_to_one")\n    result = "accepted"\nexcept pd.errors.MergeError:\n    result = "rejected"',[([1],'rejected'),([1,2],'rejected')],'validate="many_to_one"','validate="many_to_many"')
t(13,'row-filter','Filter rows with an explicit predicate','A Boolean row mask has one entry per row. Construct it from the intended column and retain only rows satisfying the stated predicate.','An inclusive threshold admits the boundary row.','frame = pd.DataFrame({"x":data})\nresult = frame.loc[frame.x>1,"x"].tolist()',[([0,1,2],[2]),([1],[])],'frame.x>1','frame.x>=1')
t(13,'deduplicate-records','Choose a duplicate policy','drop_duplicates can retain the first or last observation for a key. Specify the policy explicitly when ingestion order encodes which observation is authoritative.','Keeping the first record discards the newer replacement.','frame = pd.DataFrame(data,columns=["id","value"])\nresult = frame.drop_duplicates("id",keep="last").values.tolist()',[([[1,10],[1,20]],[[1,20]]),([[2,3]],[[2,3]])],'keep="last"','keep="first"')
t(13,'csv-roundtrip','Round-trip tabular data with a schema','CSV does not carry a complete dtype schema. This numeric example excludes the index explicitly so reading it does not create an unintended extra feature column.','Writing the index adds a new column on import.','frame = pd.DataFrame({"x":data})\nstream = io.StringIO()\nframe.to_csv(stream,index=False)\nstream.seek(0)\nresult = list(pd.read_csv(stream).columns)',[([1,2],['x']),([3],['x'])],'index=False','index=True','import io')

t(14,'group-aggregate','Aggregation reduces each group','groupby aggregation produces one output per group. Specify key sorting when deterministic output order matters and distinguish missing group keys from missing values.','Counting rows is different from summing their values.','frame = pd.DataFrame(data,columns=["group","value"])\nresult = frame.groupby("group",sort=True).value.sum().tolist()',[([['b',3],['a',1],['a',2]],[3,3]),([['a',4]],[4])],'.value.sum()','.value.count()')
t(14,'group-transform','Transform preserves row alignment','A group transform broadcasts a group-level calculation back to each original row. It differs from aggregation, whose output has one row per group.','An aggregate loses the original row-level shape.','frame = pd.DataFrame(data,columns=["group","value"])\nresult = frame.groupby("group").value.transform("mean").tolist()',[([['a',1],['a',3],['b',8]],[2,2,8]),([['a',4]],[4])],'.transform("mean")','.mean()')
t(14,'pivot-duplicates','Pivot requires a unique cell mapping','pivot maps index/column pairs to cells and requires uniqueness. pivot_table can aggregate duplicates, but doing so changes the operation and should be deliberate.','Silently averaging duplicate cells conceals a violated uniqueness contract.','frame = pd.DataFrame(data,columns=["row","column","value"])\ntry:\n    frame.pivot(index="row",columns="column",values="value")\n    result = "unique"\nexcept ValueError:\n    result = "duplicate"',[([['a','x',1],['a','x',2]],'duplicate'),([['a','x',1]],'unique')],'frame.pivot(','frame.pivot_table(')
t(14,'melt-long','Reshape wide tables to long records','melt turns measured columns into variable/value rows while retaining identifier columns. State the identifier columns so they are not accidentally treated as measurements.','Melting the identifier adds records with the wrong meaning.','frame = pd.DataFrame(data)\nresult = len(frame.melt(id_vars=["id"]))',[({'id':[1,2],'a':[3,4],'b':[5,6]},4),({'id':[1],'a':[2]},1)],'id_vars=["id"]','id_vars=[]')
t(14,'multi-index','MultiIndex keys identify hierarchical records','A MultiIndex represents compound labels. Select a complete key when the contract requests one record; selecting only one level returns a larger substructure.','Swapping key components addresses a different record or fails.','index = pd.MultiIndex.from_tuples([("a",1),("b",2)])\ns = pd.Series(data,index=index)\nresult = int(s.loc[("b",2)])',[([3,7],7),([1,9],9)],'("b",2)','("a",1)')
t(14,'rolling-window','Rolling windows encode local history','A trailing rolling mean uses the current and preceding values. min_periods defines when there is enough history to emit a value; centered windows can leak future information.','A one-element window does not smooth over two observations.','result = pd.Series(data,dtype=float).rolling(2,min_periods=1).mean().tolist()',[([2,4,8],[2,3,6]),([5],[5])],'rolling(2,','rolling(1,')
t(14,'resample-time','Resampling groups by time bins','Resample aggregates records into explicit time intervals. The bin frequency, timezone and boundary labels are part of the analytical contract.','An hourly frequency is not a daily aggregation.','index = pd.date_range("2026-01-01",periods=len(data),freq="12h")\ns = pd.Series(data,index=index)\nresult = s.resample("D").sum().tolist()',[([1,2,3,4],[3,7]),([5,6],[11])],'resample("D")','resample("12h")')
t(14,'asof-direction','As-of joins need a time direction','merge_asof matches nearby ordered keys. A backward match uses only an observation at or before the query, while a forward match can select future information.','Forward matching can leak future observations into historical features.','left = pd.DataFrame({"t":data})\nright = pd.DataFrame({"t":[0,10],"x":[1,9]})\nresult = pd.merge_asof(left,right,on="t",direction="backward").x.tolist()',[([2,8],[1,1]),([0,10],[1,9])],'direction="backward"','direction="forward"')
t(14,'copy-on-write','Version copy semantics explicitly','In pandas 2.3, enabling copy-on-write makes a derived Series write independent of its parent DataFrame. Pin this option rather than assuming behavior from another pandas release.','Disabling copy-on-write can let the view mutation update the parent.','with pd.option_context("mode.copy_on_write",True):\n    frame = pd.DataFrame({"x":data})\n    view = frame["x"]\n    view.iloc[0] = 99\n    result = frame.x.tolist()',[([1,2],[1,2]),([3],[3])],'"mode.copy_on_write",True','"mode.copy_on_write",False')
t(14,'sparse-storage','Sparse values retain an implicit fill','A sparse array stores entries different from its fill value. The fill value is part of the representation contract; sparse storage is beneficial only for suitable data distributions.','A different implicit fill changes the number of stored entries.','a = pd.arrays.SparseArray(data,fill_value=0)\nresult = int(a.sp_index.npoints)',[([0,0,2],1),([0,3,4],2)],'fill_value=0','fill_value=1')
t(14,'chunked-aggregation','Combine chunk-level sufficient statistics','A total can be computed by summing chunk totals. Combining means requires weighting by chunk counts; simply averaging chunk means fails when sizes differ.','Averaging chunk means without counts biases the overall mean.','total = sum(sum(chunk) for chunk in data)\ncount = sum(len(chunk) for chunk in data)\nresult = total/count',[([[1,3],[8]],4.0),([[2],[4]],3.0)],'total/count','sum(sum(c)/len(c) for c in data)/len(data)')
